frac{1}{x+1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0}{(\\frac{1}{0+1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264164 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1089 "q-114239" 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}}=$" 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1113 #uuid "9c771f81-c5b8-51aa-b04a-9b9d2e6048b6" 13194139533894 true] [17592186264163 1145 "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{2}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-x}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{2}]^{′}}{{[{e}^{-x}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{-x}} & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2x}{{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{[2x]^{′}}{[{e}^{-x}]^{′}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{2}{-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =2{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264165 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264166 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264167 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264168 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264169 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533894 true] [17592186264164 1041 "selection" 131